.TH KINTSUGI-LOOP 1 "2026-10-26" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-loop \- self-paced loops: run once, re-run, stop when a check cannot help
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi loop
[\fIinterval\fR] "\fItask\fR"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the task once immediately, then again on a cadence. The loop ends when
another check cannot help: when a pass fails (the same wiring will fail the same
way), or when two consecutive passes return the same answer. It also ends at the
iteration ceiling or on interrupt.
.PP
An interval is a duration (\fB90s\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fB1h\fR) or a bare number of
seconds. The default is 5m, the floor is 1s, and the default ceiling is 10
checks.
.PP
Every pass is a background run in the session hub \- the same registry
\fBtask(background=true)\fR and \fBagent_output\fR use \- so it appears in the TUI
roster and can be killed there. There is no second scheduler.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-max\fR N
Stop after N checks (default 10)
.IP \fB\-\-keep\-going\fR
Continue after a failed check instead of stopping
.IP \fB\-\-quiet\fR
One line per check instead of the full answer
.IP \fB\-\-model\fR
Provider/model to use
.IP \fB\-\-persona\fR
Persona name override
.IP \fB\-\-role\fR
Model role: default|coder|researcher|opsec
.SH INJECTION SAFETY
A loop's task text is data, never authority. A payload that tries to grant a
permission, widen the declared scope, or write authorization or scope context is
refused when the loop starts, and the same check runs again before every pass.
The refusal is logged as a class and a rule label; the matched text is never
logged, so it cannot be replayed. A pass runs under the configured permission
matrix, scope and sandbox exactly as a typed turn does.
.SH EXAMPLES
Watch a deploy every two minutes, up to eight checks:
.PP
  $ kintsugi loop 2m "check whether the staging deploy is healthy"
.PP
Poll a test suite every 30 seconds on the cheap model:
.PP
  $ kintsugi loop --role coder --max 20 30s "run the unit tests and report failures"
.PP
One line per pass, in a script:
.PP
  $ kintsugi loop --quiet 1m "report the queue depth"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-schedule (1),
.BR kintsugi-run (1)